---
<SiteLayout title="Archive — Edmund Hillary Fellowship" description="Keep up to date with the Fellowship and discover impact being created across Aotearoa and the world.">
  <div class="archive-page">
    <header class="archive-hero">
      <img class="archive-hero__image" src="/assets/archive/archive-hero-band.webp" alt="" width="1440" height="2690" />
      <h1>Archive</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="archive-section archive-section--wave" aria-labelledby="archive-organisation-news">
      <h2 id="archive-organisation-news">EHF Organisation News Archive</h2>
      <ul class="archive-carousel" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="archive-organisation-news">
        {newsCards.map((card) => <li class="archive-card">
          <a class="archive-card__image" href={card.href} tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src={card.image} alt="" width="592" height="333" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <h3><a href={card.href}>{card.title}</a></h3>
          <p>{card.date}</p>
          <a class="button-link" href={card.href} aria-label={`Read more: ${card.title}`}>Read more</a>
        </li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="archive-section archive-section--snapshots archive-section--wave" aria-labelledby="archive-fellows-news">
      <h2 id="archive-fellows-news">Fellows’ News Archive</h2>
      <ul class="archive-carousel" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="archive-fellows-news">
        {snapshotCards.map((card) => <li class="archive-card">
          <a class="archive-card__image" href={card.href} tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src={card.image} alt="" width="592" height="333" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <h3><a href={card.href} aria-label={`Impact Snapshot — ${card.month}`}>Impact Snapshot</a></h3>
          <p>{card.month}</p>
          <a class="button-link" href={card.href} aria-label={`Read full snapshot: ${card.month}`}>Read full snapshot</a>
        </li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="archive-section archive-section--reports archive-section--wave" aria-labelledby="archive-annual-reports">
      <h2 id="archive-annual-reports">Annual Reports Archive</h2>
      <div class="archive-reports">
        {archiveReports.map((report) => <article class="archive-report">
          <h3>{report.year}</h3>
          <img class="archive-report__cover" src={report.cover} alt="" width={report.coverWidth} height={report.coverHeight} loading="lazy" />
          <ul class="archive-report__documents">
            {report.documents.map((document) => <li>
              <a class="button-link" href={document.href} aria-label={`${document.label}: ${report.year}`}>{document.label}</a>
            </li>)}
          </ul>
        </article>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="archive-section archive-events" aria-labelledby="events">
      <h2 id="events">Events Archive</h2>
      <p class="archive-events__intro"><strong>Find out more about our past events, including links to any recordings that are available.</strong></p>

      <article class="event-feature">
        <h3>2025 Hillary Innovation Summit</h3>
        <ResponsiveImage class="event-feature__image" assetId={assetIdForLocalPath('/assets/images/content/archive-events-hero-social.webp')} alt="2025 Hillary Innovation Summit" width={1500} height={844} sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter)), 900px" />
        <p>The Hillary Institute &amp; Edmund Hillary Fellowship hosted the <strong>2025 Hillary Innovation Summit</strong> on <strong>17-18 February 2025</strong> in Tāmaki Makaurau Auckland. The 2025 Summit brought together up to <strong>300 local and international leaders</strong> in person over two days to explore how we can collectively build Aotearoa NZ as a basecamp for a better world and where we can lead globally. It convened Hillary Laureates, Edmund Hillary Fellows, iwi and Māori organisations, local and global investors, entrepreneurs, system designers, and public and private sector leaders. The programme featured world-leading international keynotes, innovative panel discussions, EHF Transformative Venture demos, networking, collaboration opportunities and more.</p>
        <p>With te ao Māori, wellbeing and creativity interwoven throughout, participants had the chance to engage in 15 breakout sessions to deep dive into emerging opportunities and collaborative pathways for action, focusing on the Summit’s <strong>key themes:</strong></p>
        <ResponsiveImage class="event-feature__image" assetId={assetIdForLocalPath('/assets/images/content/archive-events-key-themes.webp')} alt="2025 Hillary Innovation Summit key themes" width={1500} height={397} sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter)), 900px" />
        <p><a href="/news-blog/building-a-basecamp-for-a-better-world-begins-at-2025-hillary-innovation-summit"><strong>Read the full story for more.</strong></a></p>
        <p>The 2025 Hillary Innovation Summit programme can be <a href="/2025-summit-programme"><strong>found here.</strong></a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="event-feature">
        <h3>Summit Videos</h3>
        <p>For inspiring keynotes, panel discussion and insights from the Hillary Family, Edmund Hillary Fellows, Hillary Laureates, International &amp; NZ Leaders, plus much more, check out the videos on our <a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxTt2Nm5dTv189VJJV-yN1oWmWYH4FdrT" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>YouTube playlist</strong></a>.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="event-feature event-gallery">
        <h3>Summit Photos</h3>
        <p>Images from the 2025 Hillary Innovation Summit, captured by Erica Austin of Peanut Productions Photography. If using any of these photographs, please include the following credit: <em>2025 Hillary Innovation Summit - Erica Austin, Peanut Productions Photography.</em></p>
        <div class="summit-gallery">
          {summitGallery.map((photo) => <figure>
            <ResponsiveImage assetId={assetIdForLocalPath(photo.image)} alt={photo.alt} width={photo.width} height={photo.height} sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter)), (max-width: 1120px) 33vw, 260px" />
          </figure>)}
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="event-sessions">
        <h3>Ecosystem Sessions</h3>
        <article>
          <h4>Transformative Ventures with Global Impact - Crypto &amp; Blockchain</h4>
          <p>As part of Techweek NZ 2024, EHF convened the online event, ‘Transformative Ventures with Global Impact: Crypto &amp; Blockchain’, with Fellows <strong>Aya Miyaguchi</strong>, Executive Director of the <a href="https://ethereum.org/en/foundation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ethereum Foundation</a>, <strong>Paul Salisbury</strong>, Co-Founder and CTO of <a href="https://www.everlasting.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Everlasting</a>, and <strong>Andrew Hoppin</strong>, Co-Founder and CIO of <a href="https://www.hylafunds.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hyla Funds</a>.</p>
          <p>Aya, Paul, and Andrew are leading crypto and blockchain innovation, through transformative ventures that are focused on supporting communities and leveraging advanced technologies for good. They shared their journeys and challenges, and also explored the opportunities for how Aotearoa NZ can be a leader in crypto and blockchain for global impact.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h4>How NZ Can Be A Global Leader in Sustainable Space &amp; Aerospace</h4>
          <p>Aotearoa NZ’s aerospace &amp; space activity is on the rise, with many ventures and products offering sustainable solutions or applications. So what is the potential for NZ to be at the forefront of global sustainable space &amp; aerospace innovations, and how do we get there?</p>
          <p>In this discussion, ‘How NZ Can Be A Global Leader in Sustainable Space &amp; Aerospace’, the panel explores how Aotearoa NZ can lead the way, with insights from: <strong>Philipp Sueltrop</strong>, EHF Fellow &amp; CTO at Kea Aerospace, <strong>Max Arshavsky</strong>, CEO at Zenno Astronautics, <strong>Emeline Paat-Dahlstrom</strong>, EHF Fellow &amp; CEO at SpaceBase. Moderated by <strong>Mark Rocket</strong>, President of Aerospace New Zealand &amp; CEO at Kea Aerospace.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <ResponsiveImage class="event-feature__image" assetId={assetIdForLocalPath('/assets/images/content/archive-events-impact-springboard-banner.webp')} alt="EHF Impact Springboard" width={1500} height={750} sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter)), 900px" />
          <p>The <strong>EHF Impact Springboard</strong> was a FREE online multi-session event held over four days in February 2024 connecting Aotearoa NZ's innovation ecosystem with EHF Fellows, Hillary Laureates and NZ leaders around critical challenges facing Aotearoa NZ. Hear about EHF Fellows’ groundbreaking ventures transforming industries and systems for global impact, and from experts who are helping to elevate NZ startups onto the global stage.</p>
          <p>Watch the recording of each session below.</p>
          <h4>Impact Springboard - February 2024</h4>
          <h5>Transformative Ventures with Global Impact</h5>
          <p>A panel of Fellows share their groundbreaking ventures that are transforming industries and systems for global impact. How can Aotearoa NZ embrace the scale of opportunity these transformative ventures present?</p>
          <p><strong>Aaron McDonald</strong> | EHF Fellow | Founder Futureverse<br /><strong>Dipanwita Das</strong> | EHF Fellow | Co-founder Sorcero<br /><strong>Lovina McMurchy</strong> | EHF Fellow | COO Kry10 Limited</p>
          <h5>Going Global: Transforming NZ Startups into Global Leaders</h5>
          <p>Join a panel of local and international experts to gain insights into how to mature Aotearoa NZ’s innovation system to enable NZ businesses to scale and succeed internationally.</p>
          <p><strong>Guy Te Kiniwe Royal</strong> | Director Tuia Group<br /><strong>Anthony Lee</strong> | EHF Fellow | C100 Member<br /><strong>Marian Johnson</strong> | Ministry of Awesome</p>
          <h5>Emerging Models: Regenerative &amp; Blended Finance</h5>
          <p>EHF Fellows are developing a Climate Impact Fund for Asia Pacific Islands (CLIMAP) to support communitarian projects in the region, and test new purpose-driven finance models and instruments.</p>
          <p><strong>Satya Dontamsetti</strong> | EHF Fellow<br /><strong>Vishal Chaddha</strong> | EHF Fellow<br /><strong>Sid Sthalekar</strong> | EHF Fellow</p>
          <h5>Transforming NZ into a Low-Carbon Economy by 2050</h5>
          <p>International Climate Leader, Builder and Strategist <a href="https://www.christensenglobal.com/team/aimee-christensen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aimée Christensen</a> discusses how Aotearoa NZ can responsibly manage its transition to meet its 2050 net zero commitments in ways that affirm economic and social benefits.</p>
          <p><strong>Aimée Christensen</strong> | Hillary Laureate Founder &amp; CEO of Christensen Global Strategies<br />Interviewer: <strong>Anna Kominik</strong></p>
          <h5>Catalysing Communitarian Responses to Combat World Crises</h5>
          <p>Web 3.0 technologies are sparking new patterns of social coordination at scale. In this presentation, see how projects like <a href="https://neighbourhoods.network/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Neighbourhoods</a> (headquartered out of Aotearoa NZ) are enabling new kinds of social impact.</p>
          <p><strong>Siddharth Sthalekar</strong> | EHF Fellow<br />Founder oNeighbourhoods<br />With <strong>Camia Young</strong></p>
        </article>
      </div>

